\fs80\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s0 \li4233 \fi-2721 \ri1007 \ql \tx4233 \f0 \b \fs24 Adopted By:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 NSColorPicker\
\fs20\
\s22 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 Declared In:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 AppKit/NSColorPicking.h\
\fs20\
\fs20\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s54 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Protocol Description\
\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Together with the NSColorPickingDefault protocol, NSColorPickingCustom provides a way to add color pickers\'d0custom user interfaces for color selection\'d0to an application\'27s NSColorPanel. The NSColorPickingDefault protocol provides basic behavior for a color picker. The NSColorPicker class adopts the NSColorPickingDefault protocol. The easiest way to implement a color picker is to create a subclass of NSColorPicker and implement the NSColorPickingCustom protocol for this new class.\
\fs14\
\pard \s46 \li2310 \fi-798 \ri1007 \ql \tx2308 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 Note:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 All of NSColorPickingCustom\'27s methods must be implemented by the custom color picker.\
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Here are the standard color picking modes and mode constants (defined in \b AppKit/NSColorPanel.h\b0 ):\
\fs14\
\pard \s62 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9553 \f0 \b \fs28 Mode\tab Color Mode Constant\
\fs6\
\pard \s50 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx11541 \f1 \b0 \fs28 Grayscale-Alpha\tab NSGrayModeColorPanel\
\fi0 Red-Green-Blue\tab NSRGBModeColorPanel \
\fi0 Cyan-Yellow-Magenta-Black\tab NSCMYKModeColorPanel\
\fi0 Hue-Saturation-Brightness\tab NSHSBModeColorPanel\
\fi0 Custom palette\tab NSCustomPaletteModeColorPanel \
\fi0 Custom color list\tab NSColorListModeColorPanel \
\fi0 Color wheel\tab NSWheelModeColorPanel \
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 In grayscale-alpha, red-green-blue, cyan-magenta-yellow-black, and hue-saturation-brightness modes, the user adjusts colors by manipulating sliders. In the custom palette mode, the user can load an NSImage file (TIFF or EPS) into the NSColorPanel, then select colors from the image. In custom color list mode, the user can create and load lists of named colors. The two custom modes provide NSPopUpLists for loading and saving files. Finally, color wheel mode provides a simplified control for selecting colors. \
\fs14\
\fs28 If your color picker includes submodes, you should define a unique value for each submode. As an example, the slider picker has four values defined in the above list (NSGrayModeColorPanel, NSRGBModeColorPanel, NSCMYKModeColorPanel, and NSHSBModeColorPanel)\'d0one for each of its submodes.\
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 NSColorPickingDefault, NSColorPicker (class)\
\fs14\
