\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 {{\NeXTHelpMarker4812 \markername NS_DEV_DOCFOR:objc_method:[NSColorPickingCustom-provideNewView:];}
¬}\pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 provideNewView:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(NSView *)\b provideNewView:\b0 (BOOL)\i initialRequest\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns the view containing the color picker\'27s user interface. This message is sent to the color picker whenever the color panel attempts to display it. This may be when the panel is first presented, when the user switches pickers, or when the picker is switched through API. The argument \i initialRequest\i0  is YES only when this method is first invoked for your color picker. If \i initialRequest\i0  is YES, the method should perform any initialization required (such as lazily loading a nib file, initializing the view, or performing any other custom initialization required for your picker). The NSView returned by this method should be set to automatically resize both its width and height. \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 {{\NeXTHelpMarker5412 \markername NS_DEV_DOCFOR:objc_method:[NSColorPickingCustom-setColor:];}
¬}\pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 setColor:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(void)\b setColor:\b0 (NSColor *)\i color\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Adjusts the color picker to make \i color\i0  the currently selected color. This method is invoked on the current color picker each time NSColorPanel\'27s \b setColor:\b0  method is invoked. If \i color\i0  is actually different from the color picker\'27s color (as it would be if, for example, the user dragged a color into NSColorPanel\'27s color well), this method could be used to update the color picker\'27s color to reflect the change. \
\fs14\
\fs46\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 {{\NeXTHelpMarker6013 \markername NS_DEV_DOCFOR:objc_method:[NSColorPickingCustom-supportsMode:];}
¬}\pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 supportsMode:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(BOOL)\b supportsMode:\b0 (int)\i mode\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Returns whether or not the receiver supports the specified picking mode. This method is invoked when the NSColorPanel\'27s is first initialized: It is used to attempt to restore the user\'27s previously selected mode. It is also invoked by NSColorPanel\'27s \b setMode:\b0  method to find the color picker that supports a particular mode. See this protocol description\'27s list of the unique mode values for the standard color pickers used by the Application Kit.\
\fs14\
